.Dd August 31, 2026
.Dt KERN_BOOTCOUNT 9
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kern_get_bootcount ,
.Nm kern_bootcount_is_fw_backed
.Nd retrieve the current boot's anti-replay counter value
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/bootcount.h
.Ft uint64_t
.Fn kern_get_bootcount void
.Ft bool
.Fn kern_bootcount_is_fw_backed void
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn kern_get_bootcount
function returns the value of
.Va kern.bootcount ,
a
.Vt uint64_t
guaranteed to differ between any two boots of the system; see
.Xr bootcount 4
for the underlying counter and its trust model.
.Pp
The
.Fn kern_bootcount_is_fw_backed
function reports whether that value is firmware-backed.
Consumers requiring a genuine anti-forgery guarantee, such as
mixing the counter into an early-boot HMAC, should check this
before trusting the return value of
.Fn kern_get_bootcount .
.Pp
Both values are populated by
.Xr SYSINIT 9
at
.Dv SI_SUB_KMEM
and are safe to call from any context after that point.
Calling either function before this SYSINIT stage has run returns
zero or
.Dv false
respectively.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
if (kern_bootcount_is_fw_backed()) {
	uint64_t bc = kern_get_bootcount();
	HMAC_Update(&ctx, (uint8_t *)&bc, sizeof(bc));
}
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bootcount 4 ,
.Xr SYSINIT 9
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm kern_get_bootcount
facility was implemented as part of a Google Summer of Code 2026
project.
